[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Backend Low Level Requirements
UID: GSSC-BACKEND-LOW-LEVEL-REQUIREMENTS
VERSION: 5.0.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: TEXT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: SECTION
  PROPERTIES:
    IS_COMPOSITE: True
    PREFIX: None
    VIEW_STYLE: Narrative
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  PROPERTIES:
    PREFIX: GSSC-BLLR-
    VIEW_STYLE: Table
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: DERIVED
    TYPE: SingleChoice(True, False)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION_METHOD
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Test, Inspection)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: CHANGE_DRIVER
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: REVIEW_STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Changed, Approved, Baselined)
    REQUIRED: True
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent
    ROLE: Refines
    REVERSE_ROLE: Refined By

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-SERVICE-TRANSACTIONS
TITLE: Service Transactions

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-USER-ACCOUNTS
TITLE: User Accounts

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-LOGIN
TITLE: /login

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-1
TITLE: Login Identifiers
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take a member login as a password together with either a Username or a Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member logs in with a password and one account identifier. The identifier is a Username or the Primary Email.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-2
TITLE: Both Identifiers Invalidated
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a member login that supplies both a Username and a Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The login takes one identifier. A login that supplies both a Username and a Primary Email is invalidated.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-3
TITLE: Neither Identifier Invalidated
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a member login that supplies neither a Username nor a Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The login takes one identifier. A login that supplies neither a Username nor a Primary Email is invalidated.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-4
TITLE: Unknown Username Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a member login when the supplied Username matches no member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A Username that matches no member is not a login. The login is forbidden.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-5
TITLE: Unknown Primary Email Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a member login when the supplied Primary Email matches no member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A Primary Email that matches no member is not a login. The login is forbidden.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-6
TITLE: Password Mismatch Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a member login when the supplied Username or Primary Email matches a member and the supplied password does not match that member's stored password hash.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend compares the supplied password with the member's stored password hash. A password that does not match that hash is forbidden. This requirement does not set the hash method.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-7
TITLE: Password Match
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL log the member in when the supplied Username or Primary Email matches a member and the supplied password matches that member's stored password hash.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member login succeeds when the identifier locates the member and the password matches the stored password hash. This requirement does not set the hash method.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-8
TITLE: Login Token Issued
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL issue a Login Token when a member login succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful login yields a Login Token that a later challenge can test.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-2
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-11
TITLE: Login Token Lifetime
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take the lifetime of a Login Token from backend configuration. The configured lifetime is a number of days greater than zero. The configured lifetime defaults to seven days.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The time a Login Token remains valid is configuration. The configured lifetime is greater than zero. The configured lifetime defaults to seven days.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-5
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-LOGOUT
TITLE: /logout

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-10
TITLE: Member Logout
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL end the member login of a Login Token when that member logs out that token. A later challenge of that Login Token reports it as invalid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member ends a login by logging out that Login Token. After logout, the token no longer represents a valid login.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-4
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-CHALLENGE
TITLE: /challenge

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-9
TITLE: Login Token Challenge
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL report a challenged Login Token as valid or invalid. The report is valid for a Login Token issued for a successful member login that has not expired and has not been logged out. The report does not include the contents of the Login Token.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The challenge tells the caller whether the Login Token is valid. The report is only valid or invalid, and it does not return the token contents.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-3
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-12
TITLE: Expired Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL expire a Login Token when its lifetime has elapsed since the token was issued. A later challenge of that Login Token reports it as invalid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A Login Token stops being a valid login when its configured lifetime has elapsed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-5
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-DATA-STORAGE
TITLE: Data Storage

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-USERS
TITLE: Users

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-13
TITLE: Users Table
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store each user in a users table.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
This story keeps each user record in a table. The columns of that table are the requirements under Users Table Fields.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-118
  ROLE: Refines

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-USERS-TABLE-FIELDS
TITLE: Users Table Fields

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-14
TITLE: User Username
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a Username for each user in the users table.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Member login accepts a Username. No high-level requirement stores a Username. Each user record holds one.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-15
TITLE: User Primary Email
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a Primary Email for each user in the users table except the permanent admin account. The permanent admin account may have no Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Each user record holds the Primary Email used for login. A user account includes a Primary Email. The permanent admin account is the builtin admin account and may have no Primary Email.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-100
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-101
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-16
TITLE: User Secondary Email
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a Secondary Email for a user in the users table. The Secondary Email may be absent.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Each user record can hold a Secondary Email. The Secondary Email may be absent.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-102
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-17
TITLE: User Password Hash
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the current password hash for each user in the users table.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Each user record holds the hash used to check a login password. This requirement does not set the hash method.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-112
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-USERS-TABLE-CONSTRAINTS
TITLE: Users Table Constraints

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-18
TITLE: Unique Username
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL associate each Username in the users table with one user.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Login treats a Username as locating one user. Each stored Username belongs to one user.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-19
TITLE: Unique Primary Email
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL associate each Primary Email in the users table with one user.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Login treats a Primary Email as locating one user. Each stored Primary Email belongs to one user.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-WEB-SECURITY
TITLE: Web Security

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-PERMANENT-ADMIN
TITLE: Permanent Admin

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-20
TITLE: Admin Username
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL read the permanent admin username from the .env file. The username defaults to admin.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The permanent admin account takes its username from the .env file. No high-level requirement defines this account.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-21
TITLE: Admin Password
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL read the permanent admin password from the .env file. The password defaults to 1234.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The permanent admin account takes its password from the .env file. No high-level requirement defines this account.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-22
TITLE: Admin Account Enabled
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL read a flag from the .env file that enables the permanent admin account. The flag defaults to false.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The .env file decides whether the permanent admin account is created. The flag defaults to false.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-23
TITLE: Permanent Admin Account
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL create a permanent admin account when the .env flag enables it. The account is a user with the configured username, a current password hash of the configured password, and the configured admin email when that email is provided. The admin email is read from the .env file and defaults to empty. An empty admin email leaves the Primary Email unset. When the configured username already exists, the backend replaces that user's password hash and leaves the Primary Email and Secondary Email unchanged.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No high-level requirement defines this account. The account is a user so the configured admin can log in. This requirement does not set the hash method. The Secondary Email is unset. The Primary Email is the configured admin email, and the permanent admin email is unset unless it is provided. An existing user keeps both email values when the password hash is replaced.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-24
TITLE: Admin Account Disabled
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL leave the permanent admin account uncreated when the .env flag is disabled. When that account already exists, the backend leaves the user and the user's password hash unchanged.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The flag defaults to false, so the permanent admin account is not created unless the flag enables it. Disabling the flag leaves an existing permanent admin account in place and does not change its password hash.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]
